</html:p>
                <html:p>
    Questions this page should answer:
    <html:ul><html:li>The format: <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[(Az) \circ  (Bz) = Cz]]></fr:tex>, the instance and witness split, and what "satisfying" means.</html:li>
        <html:li>Sparsity, and why the prover's cost is an MSM or a sparse-polynomial commitment rather than an FFT.</html:li>
        <html:li>Relaxed and committed R1CS, the variants folding needs.</html:li>
        <html:li>The cost of a range check or a bit decomposition here, compared with a <fr:link href="/dhsorens-002W/" title="Lookup Arguments" uri="https://derekhsorensen.com/dhsorens-002W/" display-uri="dhsorens-002W" type="local">lookup</fr:link> in a Plonkish system.</html:li>
