                <fr:title text="Plonkish Arithmetisation">Plonkish Arithmetisation</fr:title>
              </fr:frontmatter>
              <fr:mainmatter>
                <html:p>
    Gate constraints plus a wiring argument, with lookups bolted on. "Plonkish" is used loosely across implementations, so the term needs a precise statement of what it covers.
</html:p>
                <html:p>
    Questions this page should answer:
    <html:ul><html:li>Gate constraints and selectors; custom gates and what raising the degree costs.</html:li>
        <html:li>Copy constraints via a <fr:link href="/dhsorens-002X/" title="Permutation, Grand-Product, and Memory Arguments" uri="https://derekhsorensen.com/dhsorens-002X/" display-uri="dhsorens-002X" type="local">permutation argument</fr:link> — the mechanism that distinguishes Plonkish from AIR.</html:li>
        <html:li>Lookup tables in the halo2 sense: regions, fixed columns, and the developer-facing cost model.</html:li>
        <html:li>Preprocessing: what is fixed at setup and what varies per instance.</html:li>
        <html:li>Where Plonkish and <fr:link href="/dhsorens-002U/" title="AIR" uri="https://derekhsorensen.com/dhsorens-002U/" display-uri="dhsorens-002U" type="local">AIR</fr:link> genuinely differ, once cross-table lookups are available to both.</html:li></html:ul></html:p>
              </fr:mainmatter>
