                <fr:title text="CCS and the Unified View">CCS and the Unified View</fr:title>
              </fr:frontmatter>
              <fr:mainmatter>
                <html:p>
    Customisable constraint systems, proposed as the generalisation that has R1CS, Plonkish, and AIR as instances. Worth understanding both as a claim about expressiveness and as the format HyperNova folds.
</html:p>
                <html:p>
    Questions this page should answer:
    <html:ul><html:li>The definition, and the explicit embeddings of the three formats into it.</html:li>
        <html:li>What the unification buys: one folding scheme, one commitment interface, one soundness proof.</html:li>
        <html:li>What it costs — where a CCS encoding is asymptotically or concretely worse than the native format.</html:li>
        <html:li>Whether the same unification is the right structuring principle for a formal library, or whether <fr:link href="/dhsorens-0040/" title="ArkLib" uri="https://derekhsorensen.com/dhsorens-0040/" display-uri="dhsorens-0040" type="local">ArkLib</fr:link>'s per-system files are better.</html:li></html:ul></html:p>
              </fr:mainmatter>
