                <fr:title text="Lookup Arguments">Lookup Arguments</fr:title>
              </fr:frontmatter>
              <fr:mainmatter>
                <html:p>
    Modern zkVMs are mostly lookups: instruction semantics, range checks, bitwise operations, and memory consistency all become table queries. This is where the prover's time goes, so it is where the interesting engineering is.
</html:p>
                <html:p>
    Questions this page should answer:
    <html:ul><html:li>The logarithmic-derivative identity (logUp) and why it replaced grand-product multiset checks.</html:li>
        <html:li>logUp-GKR: applying <fr:link href="/dhsorens-002Q/" title="The Sumcheck Protocol" uri="https://derekhsorensen.com/dhsorens-002Q/" display-uri="dhsorens-002Q" type="local">sumcheck</fr:link> to the fraction identity to avoid committing to <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[O(m)]]></fr:tex> field elements.</html:li>
        <html:li>Lasso: the lookup relation as <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[a = M \cdot  T]]></fr:tex> with <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[M]]></fr:tex> sparse, and decomposability for tables of size <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[2^{64}]]></fr:tex> and beyond.</html:li>
        <html:li>logup* and the small-table indexed case.</html:li>
        <html:li>The "lookup singularity" claim from 2023 — how much of it held, measured in real zkVM benchmarks.</html:li>
        <html:li>What a lookup argument's soundness proof actually requires, and what the <fr:link href="https://eprint.iacr.org/2024/1841" type="external">Jolt semantics verification</fr:link> found.</html:li></html:ul></html:p>
                <html:p>
    Sources: <fr:link href="https://www.zkm.io/blog/the-logup-gkr-protocol" type="external">The logUp-GKR protocol</fr:link>, <fr:link href="https://a16zcrypto.com/posts/article/introducing-lasso-and-jolt/" type="external">Introducing Lasso and Jolt</fr:link>, <fr:link href="https://eprint.iacr.org/2025/946" type="external">logup*</fr:link>, <fr:link href="https://eprint.iacr.org/2024/1841" type="external">Verifying Jolt zkVM Lookup Semantics</fr:link>.
</html:p>
              </fr:mainmatter>
